:: Sister studying [interaction] {"position":"400,2100","size":"100,100"}
/* Talk scene ("Chat with her", Define Interactions): $sister studying in her room at home.
   1 (the focus tree) and 2 (out loud) always.
   3 (the calculus wall): before sister_fakingIt. The last line changes once sister_planningAhead is done.
   4 (sleeping better): after sister_focusIsKey, before sister_partyAnimal. The deal from Focus Is Key holds, so nobody says it.
   5 (a math person now): after sister_sheMadeIt, before sister_conflictingFeelings. Mentions her tutoring if $sister.flags.isTutoring.
   6 (the party question): after sister_partyAnimal, before sister_conflictingFeelings. She remembers nothing of that night.
   7 (the door, +1 SisterLust if I close it): after sister_conflictingFeelings.
   8 (her case study): after sister_internshipSeason. */
<<silently>>
<<set _variants to [1, 2]>>
<<if !setup.questDone("sister_fakingIt")>><<run _variants.push(3)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("sister_focusIsKey") && !setup.questDone("sister_partyAnimal")>><<run _variants.push(4)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("sister_sheMadeIt") && !setup.questDone("sister_conflictingFeelings")>><<run _variants.push(5)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("sister_partyAnimal") && !setup.questDone("sister_conflictingFeelings")>><<run _variants.push(6)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("sister_conflictingFeelings")>><<run _variants.push(7)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("sister_internshipSeason")>><<run _variants.push(8)>><</if>>
<<set _pick to setup.pickTalkScene("Sister studying", _variants)>>
<</silently>>
<<DisplayActivity $sister 500>>
<<switch _pick>>

/* 1: The focus tree */
<<case 1>>
$sister.callName is at her desk with a textbook open in front of her and her phone lying face up next to it. On the screen there's a little cartoon sapling with a countdown underneath, 18:42 and falling. When I come in, she points at me without looking up, the way you'd point at a dog that's thinking about jumping on the couch.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Don't make me touch my phone. If I touch my phone, the tree dies." },
{ who: $player, text: "What tree?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "My focus tree. If I study for twenty-five minutes it grows, and if I pick up the phone it dies and the app shows me a sad little stump. It's incredibly judgmental, and I love it." },
{ text: "She nudges the screen sideways with one knuckle, very carefully, so it doesn't count as touching. Her forest is a grid of tiny trees, and about a third of them are brown stumps." },
{ who: $player, text: "What happened to those?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "That one was the group chat, and that one was a sale on boots, and that one..." },
{ text: "She squints at it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Honestly, no idea. Something stupid, they all died for something stupid. It's a graveyard of my bad decisions, and somehow that's the most motivating thing on my phone." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I sit down on her bed and keep my mouth shut, which she seems to think is the nicest thing I've done for her all month. Eleven minutes in, my own phone buzzes in my pocket. She turns around in her chair and stares at me until I put it face down on the blanket.

When the timer runs out, the sapling turns into a fat little pine with a squirrel in it. She holds the phone up for me to admire like she grew it herself. Then she spends the next ten minutes on that same phone, as a reward.

/* 2: Out loud */
<<case 2>>
I can hear her before I open the door. She's reading to herself, quietly and fast, and every few sentences she stops, shuts her eyes and says the same thing again without looking at the page.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Who are you talking to in here?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Myself. If I say something out loud three times, it stays put. Don't laugh, I got a ninety-one on the last quiz doing exactly this." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm not laughing. Want me to quiz you?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "God, yes, please. Ask me anything from chapter six, except the pricing part. I haven't gotten to the pricing part yet." },
{ text: "She hands me her index cards. She gets the first four before I've finished reading the questions out, and she looks a little insulted that I bothered to ask." },
{ who: $player, text: "What's a target market?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "A target market is the group of people who... no, wait, it's the specific group of... hang on. I knew this an hour ago." },
{ text: "She closes her eyes, mutters her way back to the start of the paragraph and gets it word for word." },
{ who: $sister, text: "See? It's all in there. Sometimes I just have to take the scenic route to get to it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Read her the pricing part">>
I take the book off her desk and read her the next section out loud, and because it's the driest thing I've ever held in my hands, I read it like a movie trailer. I get about four lines into penetration pricing before she slides off her chair and onto the carpet, laughing so hard she has to hold onto the desk leg.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Stop, please. It does not say 'in a world where margins are thin'. I'm looking at the page, it doesn't say that." },
{ who: $player, text: "It's implied. You have to read between the lines." },
{ who: $sister, text: "If that voice is how I end up remembering this, I'm going to hear it in the middle of the exam and laugh out loud, and it'll be your fault." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She makes me read the rest of the chapter in my normal voice. She still mouths 'in a world' at me every time a new term comes up, and by the end she knows the whole section on pricing, which is more than she knew when I walked in.
<</linkreplace>>

/* 3: The calculus wall (before sister_fakingIt) */
<<case 3>>
Her calculus book is open on the desk. $sister.callName is lying on the floor next to the desk, flat on her back, staring at the ceiling. In the margin next to problem fourteen she has written WHY in big letters, underlined it twice and drawn a small skull.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Is the book winning?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "The book won an hour ago. I'm only lying down here so it can't take the floor too." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Do you know what $prof.callName said today? He called limits 'intuitive', out loud, to a room full of actual human beings." },
{ who: $player, text: "Want me to take a look?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "If you explain it and I still don't get it, I'll have to move to another state and change my name. Just so you know what's at stake." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Get down on the floor with her">>
I lie down next to her with the book held up over both of us and a pen I find under her bed. We do problem fourteen on the back of a pizza flyer. The first time I explain it, she nods along without hearing a word. The second time, she argues with me. The third time, she goes very quiet.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Wait. So it doesn't matter what happens at the actual number, only what happens on the way there?" },
{ who: $player, text: "That's it, that's the whole trick." },
{ who: $sister, text: "That's so stupid. Why didn't he just say that? Why did he say 'intuitive' and then write a whole wall of Greek?" },
{ text: "She snatches the flyer and writes it down in her own words, under the pizza coupon, and draws a little arrow walking up to a door." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if setup.questDone("sister_planningAhead")>>
Before I go, she asks if I really think she can pass. I tell her I'm sure of it. It's the most honest thing I've said to her all week.
<<else>>
Before I go, she asks if I really think she can pass. I tell her yes. She gives me the look she used to give me when I was the only one in the house who could fix the wifi, and she believes me.
<</if>>
<</linkreplace>>

/* 4: Sleeping better (after sister_focusIsKey, before sister_partyAnimal) */
<<case 4>>
She's actually working. Her notes are in neat rows for once, every problem boxed, and she's humming something under her breath while she writes. A week ago she looked like she'd been studying inside a wind tunnel.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "You look awake." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I am awake! I slept nine hours last night, which hasn't happened since I had the flu in middle school. I just lay down and that was it, gone, like somebody pulled my plug out of the wall." },
{ text: "Then she hears herself. Her ears go pink first, then her neck, and she turns back to her notes very fast." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Don't." },
{ who: $player, text: "I didn't say anything." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You were about to, I could see it on your face. We made a deal, and that deal doesn't expire." },
{ who: $player, text: "I was going to say nice work on problem six." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Oh. Well, thank you. It is a very good problem six." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She keeps her back to me for a while after that, but she goes on humming, only quieter. I sit on her bed and check problem six, which is right, and problem seven, which isn't. I let her find seven on her own. She does, eventually, and swears at it in a whisper.

/* 5: A math person now (after sister_sheMadeIt, before sister_conflictingFeelings) */
<<case 5>>
The calculus test is stuck to the wall above her desk with four strips of washi tape, B plus facing out. Someone has added a gold star sticker next to the professor's 'much improved', and then drawn a tiny crown on the star.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Don't say anything about the crown, the crown was earned. I'm a math person now." },
{ who: $player, text: "Since when are you a math person?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Since the B plus, and it's on the wall, which makes it official. You can't argue with the wall." },
{ text: "She's doing economics homework now, a supply and demand graph, and she walks me through it with total confidence. The demand curve is going the wrong way." },
{ who: $player, text: "Your demand curve is upside down." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Real math people make mistakes constantly, that's how you can tell they're doing math. The ones who never make mistakes just aren't doing any." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if $sister.flags.isTutoring>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Also, I have a student now, a freshman named Tyler, and he calls derivatives 'the little guys'." },
{ who: $player, text: "Did you correct him?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Why would I? It's working for him. He got a C on the last quiz, and if you'd met Tyler, you'd know that a C from him is close to a miracle." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<</if>>

She flips the curve around with a lot of muttering. When she's done, she leans back and looks up at the test on the wall for a moment, the way some people look at a photo of somewhere they went on vacation.

/* 6: The party question (after sister_partyAnimal, before sister_conflictingFeelings) */
<<case 6>>
She's reading, or at least she's holding a book open at the right height for reading. The page doesn't turn the whole time I'm standing in the doorway. When she finally notices me, she shuts the book on her finger.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Hey. Can I ask you something weird?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Weirder than usual?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "The night of the party. When I got home. Did I... say anything? Do anything stupid? Because I remember the shots, and I remember the Uber guy had a bobblehead of a goat on his dashboard, and after that it's just... nothing. And then it's morning." },
{ text: "She's trying to make it sound like a joke. Her thumb is working at the corner of the page, folding it down and smoothing it out again." },
{ who: $player, text: "You told me you loved me, and then you told the fridge you loved it more, and then you fell asleep with one shoe on." },
{ who: $sister, text: "The fridge? Seriously?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You were very sincere with the fridge." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay, that's embarrassing, but that's fine. That's normal drunk stuff, everybody loves a fridge at two in the morning." },
{ text: "She laughs, and her shoulders come down a little. She opens the book again." },
{ who: $sister, text: "It's just, I keep having these... never mind. It's stupid." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I don't ask what she keeps having. I tell her the goat was probably a good omen, and she throws a pen at me. For the rest of the time I'm in her room she stays on that same page, and every time I move, she looks up.

/* 7: The door (after sister_conflictingFeelings) */
<<case 7>>
She's sitting up in bed with her laptop on her knees and a highlighter cap between her teeth. When I come in, she pulls her feet up to make room for me at the end of the mattress, the way she's done a thousand times. Then her eyes go past me, to the open door.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "So, uh. Question. Do we close the door now? When you're in here?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Do you want it closed?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "I don't know! That's why I'm asking. I've been leaving it open, and then I thought, isn't it weirder if I leave it open? Like I'm making a point? And then I thought about it way too much, and now I'm asking you, like an idiot." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Forget it. Sit. Quiz me on supply chains. Supply chains are very safe." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<div id="sister-study-door" class="choices">
	<div>
		<<link "Close the door">>
			<<replace "#sister-study-door">>
				I get up again and push it shut. The latch clicks, very loud in the quiet room. She looks at the door, not at me.

				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs = [
				{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Okay. Supply chains." },
				{ text: "She reads me the first question in a voice that's a little higher than her normal one. Somewhere around the third question, her foot finds my leg under the blanket and stays there, and she doesn't mention it, so neither do I." },
				{ text: "Out in the hall, $mom.callName's footsteps come up the stairs. $sister.callName stops in the middle of a word. She doesn't move until they've gone past and a door closes at the other end of the house." },
				{ who: $sister, text: "...Just-in-time inventory. Where was I?" },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterLust" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<div>
		<<link "Leave it open">>
			<<replace "#sister-study-door">>
				I sit down and leave the door where it is. She lets out a breath and starts reading me questions. She looks relieved, and then, when she thinks I'm busy with her notes, a little disappointed. She gets the next four questions wrong, which she never does with supply chains.
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
</div>

/* 8: Her case study (after sister_internshipSeason) */
<<case 8>>
She's at her desk with her internship lanyard still around her neck, which she's been told twice she doesn't need to wear at home. The document on her laptop is called 'Case Study FINAL final (2)'.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Perfect timing, sit down. I need to interview you." },
{ who: $player, text: "For what?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "For my small business class. We have to analyze a local company, and everybody else picked the bakery on Main Street. Six people! That poor woman is going to get interviewed to death." },
{ text: "She picks up a highlighter and holds it under my chin like a microphone." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So, Mister CEO, what would you say your company's mission is?" },
{ who: $player, text: "I guess we help people feel better at work. They're calmer, and they're a lot easier to get along with." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Ooh, that's actually good. I'm writing that down." },
{ text: "She types it word for word, reads it back to me, and then adds a line of her own about employee wellbeing being at the heart of everything we do. She asks if that part's true. I tell her it's very true." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Last question, and I asked the bakery lady too, so you have to answer: what's your secret ingredient? Hers is butter." },
{ who: $player, text: "Good people, and really good ventilation." },
{ who: $sister, text: "That's so boring. I'm putting butter." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She asks if she can put a picture of the office on the title page. I tell her sure, as long as it's taken from the street.

<</switch>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 1>>

<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Leave her to the books" $player.location.passage>><</link>></div>
